// in base/ and every overlay, one entry per document per location. The
// manifests are never rendered, so an entry says where a resource is
// declared, not what a kustomize build would make of it.
Resources []ResourceRef `json:"resources,omitempty"`

// Secrets are the secret-bearing resources found in the component's
// manifests — shared components in practice, but a service declaring one
// is worth surfacing too.
Secrets []SecretRef `json:"secrets,omitempty"`

// SecretRefs are the secrets the component references without owning: a
// binding's credentials, a connection string provisioned outside the
// repository. Owning (Secrets) and referencing are different claims — a
// referenced secret that exists nowhere is exactly the gap an operator
// needs to see, not a secret this repository declares.
SecretRefs []SecretReference `json:"secretRefs,omitempty"`

